# The Spanish Economy in Data Frames

```elixir
Mix.install([
  # To try a local checkout use {:inex, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")} instead
  {:inex, "~> 0.1.0"},
  {:kino_explorer, "~> 0.1"},
  {:kino_vega_lite, "~> 0.1"}
])
```

## Setup

This notebook combines several INE operations to take the pulse of the Spanish economy:
inflation (CPI), unemployment (EPA) and growth (quarterly national accounts), using Explorer to
transform the data and VegaLite to plot it.

```elixir
alias Explorer.DataFrame, as: DF
alias Explorer.Series, as: S
alias VegaLite, as: Vl

require Explorer.DataFrame
```

## Inflation by Spending Group

Table `76125` holds the national CPI by ECOICOP group. Let's get the annual change (`data_type: 74`)
of every group (`cpi_group: :all`):

```elixir
cpi_groups =
  Inex.Tables.observations_as_data_frame!(76125,
    filters: [data_type: 74, cpi_group: :all],
    observation_start: ~D[2024-01-01]
  )
  |> DF.rename(%{"Grupos ECOICOP" => "group"})
  |> DF.select(["date", "group", "value", "data_type"])
```

Flash estimates (`"Avance"`) only include the general index, so we take the latest month with
final data for every group:

```elixir
last_final_date =
  cpi_groups
  |> DF.filter(data_type == "Definitivo")
  |> then(& &1["date"])
  |> S.max()

latest_groups =
  cpi_groups
  |> DF.filter(date == ^last_final_date and group != "Índice general")
  |> DF.sort_by(desc: value)

Vl.new(width: 600, height: 400, title: "CPI annual change by group - #{last_final_date}")
|> Vl.data_from_values(latest_groups)
|> Vl.mark(:bar)
|> Vl.encode_field(:x, "value", type: :quantitative, title: "%")
|> Vl.encode_field(:y, "group", type: :nominal, sort: "-x", title: nil, axis: [label_limit: 400])
|> Vl.encode(:color,
  condition: [test: "datum.value < 0", value: "#d62728"],
  value: "#1f77b4"
)
```

## Regional Inflation Heatmap

Table `76136` has the CPI by autonomous community. A heatmap shows at a glance which regions are
running hotter:

```elixir
regional =
  Inex.Tables.observations_as_data_frame!(76136,
    filters: [data_type: 74, cpi_group: 304092, ccaa: :all],
    observation_start: ~D[2025-01-01]
  )
  |> DF.rename(%{"Comunidades y Ciudades Autónomas" => "region"})
  |> DF.select(["date", "region", "value"])

Vl.new(width: 700, height: 450, title: "CPI annual change by region (%)")
|> Vl.data_from_values(regional)
|> Vl.mark(:rect)
|> Vl.encode_field(:x, "date", type: :ordinal, time_unit: :yearmonth, title: nil)
|> Vl.encode_field(:y, "region", type: :nominal, title: nil)
|> Vl.encode_field(:color, "value", type: :quantitative, scale: [scheme: :orangered], title: "%")
|> Vl.encode_field(:tooltip, "value", type: :quantitative)
```

## Unemployment by Region

The labour force survey (EPA) table `65334` has the unemployment rate by sex, age and region.
Let's take both sexes (`454`) and all ages (`15668`) for every region, and compare the latest
quarter with the same quarter of the previous year:

```elixir
unemployment =
  Inex.Tables.observations_as_data_frame!(65334,
    filters: [sex: 454, age_total: 15668, ccaa: :all],
    last: 5
  )
  |> DF.rename(%{"Comunidades y Ciudades Autónomas" => "region"})
  |> DF.select(["date", "region", "value"])

[first_date, latest_date] = [S.min(unemployment["date"]), S.max(unemployment["date"])]

comparison =
  unemployment
  |> DF.filter(date == ^first_date or date == ^latest_date)
  |> DF.mutate(quarter: cast(date, :string))

Vl.new(width: 600, height: 450, title: "Unemployment rate by region (%)")
|> Vl.data_from_values(comparison)
|> Vl.mark(:point, filled: true, size: 80)
|> Vl.encode_field(:x, "value", type: :quantitative, title: "%")
|> Vl.encode_field(:y, "region", type: :nominal, sort: "-x", title: nil)
|> Vl.encode_field(:color, "quarter", type: :nominal)
```

## Growth and Unemployment: Okun's Law

Okun's law says that when the economy grows faster, unemployment falls. Let's check it with the
GDP annual growth (`CNTR6654`) and the unemployment rate (`EPA452434`), both quarterly. The wide
format gives us one row per quarter:

```elixir
quarterly =
  Inex.Series.observations_as_data_frame!(["CNTR6654", "EPA452434"],
    observation_start: ~D[2002-01-01],
    rename: %{"CNTR6654" => "gdp_growth", "EPA452434" => "unemployment"}
  )
  |> DF.drop_nil()
```

Explorer computes the year-on-year change of the unemployment rate (in percentage points) by
shifting the series four quarters:

```elixir
okun =
  quarterly
  |> DF.mutate(unemployment_change: unemployment - shift(unemployment, 4))
  |> DF.drop_nil()
  |> DF.mutate(year: year(date))
```

```elixir
Vl.new(width: 500, height: 400, title: "Okun's law in Spain (2003-today)")
|> Vl.data_from_values(okun)
|> Vl.layers([
  Vl.new()
  |> Vl.mark(:circle, size: 60, opacity: 0.8)
  |> Vl.encode_field(:x, "gdp_growth", type: :quantitative, title: "GDP annual growth (%)")
  |> Vl.encode_field(:y, "unemployment_change",
    type: :quantitative,
    title: "Change in unemployment rate (pp)"
  )
  |> Vl.encode_field(:color, "year", type: :quantitative, scale: [scheme: :viridis])
  |> Vl.encode_field(:tooltip, "date", type: :temporal),
  Vl.new()
  |> Vl.mark(:line, color: :firebrick)
  |> Vl.transform(regression: "unemployment_change", on: "gdp_growth")
  |> Vl.encode_field(:x, "gdp_growth", type: :quantitative)
  |> Vl.encode_field(:y, "unemployment_change", type: :quantitative)
])
```

The correlation confirms the negative relationship:

```elixir
S.correlation(okun["gdp_growth"], okun["unemployment_change"])
```
